R=rows('''
搬家前一天，我和朋友约好下午两点见。他来帮我搬几个重箱子，我已经订好了车，司机说两点半以前要出发去下一个地方。我把时间发给朋友，他回复“没问题”，于是没有再找第二个人。|The day before moving, a friend and I agreed to meet at two. He’d help with the heavy boxes. I’d booked a vehicle whose driver had to leave for another job by half past two. My friend replied “no problem” to the time, so I didn’t ask anyone else.
第二天，两点过了，门外还没人。我给他打电话，没有接。我最初以为他在路上，不方便看手机，就先整理小东西。到了两点二十，我不能再等，去问邻居能不能帮十分钟。邻居把重箱子搬上楼，我送司机离开时，才松了一口气。|At two the next day, nobody arrived. I called, but he didn’t answer. At first I thought he was travelling and couldn’t check his phone, so I sorted smaller items. At twenty past two I couldn’t wait longer and asked a neighbour for ten minutes of help. Once the heavy boxes were upstairs and the driver left, I finally breathed easier.
三点，朋友终于来了。他说临时开会，手机留在桌上，没有机会看到电话。我相信那场会议不是他故意安排的，但还是生气。既然他已经答应了两点到，我就在根据这个答复做安排。没有新消息，我不知道原来的安排还算不算。|My friend finally arrived at three. He said a meeting had come up and his phone had stayed on his desk. I believed he hadn’t deliberately scheduled it, but I was still angry. His agreement to arrive at two had shaped my plans. Without an update, I didn’t know whether that agreement still held.
他想马上开始做事，我请他先听我说完。我没有说他从来不可靠，也没有把这次迟到说成整个友谊都没有意义。我只说明两次电话没接以后，我为什么没能早点找别人。他听完，承认不该以为开完会再解释就够了。|He wanted to start helping immediately, but I asked him to hear me out. I didn’t say he’d never been reliable or that our friendship meant nothing. I explained why the unanswered calls had delayed asking someone else. He acknowledged that explaining after the meeting hadn’t been enough.
后来，我们一起把剩下的书放上书架。他先问我按什么顺序放，没有像上次那样只按颜色排。整理这些书不能让司机回来，也不能把那个小时拿回来，不过至少把眼前没完成的事做好了。我仍然有点累，但不用再一边做一边生气。|Later we put the remaining books on the shelf together. He asked which order I wanted instead of sorting just by colour as before. Unpacking couldn’t bring the driver or that hour back, but it finished the remaining work. I was still tired but no longer working while angry.
晚上，我给邻居发消息谢谢他，也把借来的工具还了。朋友问下周还需要他做什么，我没有马上又交给他一件大事，只说现在没有新的安排，有变化再联系。愿意继续相处，不等于当天就要重新保证什么。|That evening I thanked the neighbour and returned the borrowed tools. When my friend asked what he could do next week, I didn’t immediately assign another big task. I said there was no new plan yet and we’d keep in touch. Continuing the friendship didn’t mean making a new promise that day.
几天后想起这次经历，我更清楚自己在乎的是哪一点。我可以接受朋友偶尔来不了，也知道工作有时会突然变。可如果已经答应，就不能把别人正在等这件事忘掉。早一点联络并不能解决所有冲突，却能让对方根据真实情况作出选择，而不是一直猜。|A few days later I understood what mattered to me. I could accept a friend occasionally being unable to come and work changing unexpectedly. But once you’ve agreed, you can’t forget the other person is waiting. Early contact won’t solve every conflict, but it lets them act on the actual situation instead of guessing.
''')
